00:17:30.797 --> 00:17:32.770
but I've been picking up on some themes

00:17:32.770 --> 00:17:35.464
and I'll tell you I hate
how many people reverse it.

00:17:35.464 --> 00:17:37.484
I watch a lot of parents that are like,

00:17:37.484 --> 00:17:39.550
you know literally like soccer,

00:17:39.550 --> 00:17:41.802
they're like, oh I dunno
Ricky, if you're gonna be okay,

00:17:41.802 --> 00:17:43.194
eh, you know Johnny's really good,

00:17:43.194 --> 00:17:44.705
like no self-esteem building,

00:17:44.705 --> 00:17:47.584
and then they play,
they lose eight-nothing,

00:17:47.584 --> 00:17:49.324
and they're like Ricky,
you did a great job!

00:17:49.324 --> 00:17:51.415
It's literally the fuckin'
reverse of what I want!

00:17:51.415 --> 00:17:54.340
Which is, like, India,
you could be the greatest

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:57.172
operator of a museum in
the history of all time,

00:17:57.172 --> 00:17:58.613
and then when you have your first exhibit,

00:17:58.613 --> 00:17:59.495
if it doesn't go well,

00:17:59.495 --> 00:18:00.865
you say, look, it didn't go well,

00:18:00.865 --> 00:18:02.885
and let's backtrack and figure out why,

00:18:02.885 --> 00:18:04.046
and then I would give her,

00:18:04.046 --> 00:18:06.461
'cause my little India I
know how she likes to read,

00:18:06.461 --> 00:18:09.803
I give her a book of like
the guy or the girl who

00:18:09.803 --> 00:18:11.848
started three business and failed but then

00:18:11.848 --> 00:18:13.752
on the fourth one figured out
the learnings from the three

00:18:13.752 --> 00:18:15.934
and killed it like the KFC guy.

00:18:17.084 --> 00:18:20.853
Encouragement matters, but
reality matters just as much.

00:18:20.853 --> 00:18:23.151
And you have to create
friction amongst those two

00:18:23.151 --> 00:18:24.684
to create the perfect storm

00:18:24.684 --> 00:18:26.703
for the young and moldable minds.

00:18:26.703 --> 00:18:29.133
And the old and moldable minds.

